  "issue_title": "[bug] Completion cache persists transient empty/error responses, freezing a one-off failure into a permanent 0 score",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\n`CachedPool.chat` (`src/trinity/llm/cache.py`) writes **every** miss result to disk, with no quality gate:\n\n```python\nresult = await self._pool.chat(model, messages, ...)\nself._cache.put(key, self._record_from(result))   # persists ANY result, including errors\nreturn result\n```\n\nThe wrapped `OpenRouterPool._parse_completion` returns a non-answer sentinel on an HTTP-200-with-no-completion \u2014 a moderation block, an upstream-error surfaced as 200, or a non-JSON CDN body:\n\n```python\nreturn ChatResult(model=..., text=\"\", finish_reason=\"error\", raw=data)\n```\n\nThese are **transient**. But the cache persists the empty record and re-serves it for every future identical request. Concrete sequence (`temperature=0.0`, cache enabled):\n\n1. Rep 1 hits a transient empty response \u2192 `ChatResult(text=\"\", finish_reason=\"error\")`. The grader scores it **0** (no extractable answer). `put()` stores the empty record under the request key.\n2. Rep 2 and every later `--single-reps` rep and every subsequent run: `get()` **hits**, returns the cached `text=\"\"` for **$0**, and the task scores **0 forever**.\n\nSo the cache converts a one-off transient failure into a *permanent wrong score* for that item \u2014 the exact hazard the module docstring says it exists to avoid (\"Serving those reps from one cache entry would \u2026 silently turn a majority into a single sample\"). It also reports bogus `tokens_saved` for a completion that was never a real answer. This is distinct from the earlier openrouter empty-completion fix (which makes the *parse* degrade gracefully); here the defect is that `cache.py` then **persists and re-serves** that sentinel.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n- *Expected:* a transient empty/error completion is not cached, so a later retry issues a fresh call and can get the real answer.\n- *Actual:* the empty/error result is cached and re-served indefinitely, pinning the item to a 0 score.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\n```python\n# stub pool returns finish_reason=\"error\", text=\"\" on call 1, then a real answer on call 2\ncp = CachedPool(pool, ResponseCache(tmp))\nr1 = await cp.chat(\"m\", msgs, temperature=0.0)   # error, text=\"\"\nr2 = await cp.chat(\"m\", msgs, temperature=0.0)   # served the cached \"\" -- pool NOT called again\n```\n\nThe fix should skip caching a result whose `finish_reason == \"error\"` or whose `text` is blank; skipping only forces a fresh call next time and can never return a wrong answer.\n\n**Environment**\n- Python version: 3.10+\n- GPU: not required (pure cache logic; a temp dir stands in for the cache)\n- Commit hash: current `main`\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-12T19:23:29.000Z",
